{
  "texts": [
    {
      "content": "The Noctis Spheres are photosensitive structures made of vegetal chitin enriched with ferric minerals.",
      "left": "549px",
      "top": "311px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Their reddish stems circulate luminescent fluids that stabilize the interior,",
      "left": "675px",
      "top": "354px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "while at dusk they store starlight, acting as natural archives of celestial landscapes.",
      "left": "637px",
      "top": "393px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Ecologically, they function as luminous signals for nocturnal pollinators and",
      "left": "665px",
      "top": "435px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "as microhabitats for translucent invertebrates, also indicating soils rich in iron and manganese.",
      "left": "592px",
      "top": "478px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
